# A halftone sun that breathes: each dot's size comes from its distance to the middle.
#   ./intent svg examples/art/halftone-sun.intent --after "wait 400" --style dots
# The square root gives the distance; a ramp of characters, from "@" to ".", gives the ink.

The board is 44 wide and 30 high.
Dots have an x (number), a y (number), a far (decimal), a look (text) and a hue (text).
At the start there is a dot for every x from 1 to 44 and every y from 1 to 30, whose far is 0, whose look is " " and whose hue is "yellow".
The glow starts at 0.

Every 100 milliseconds, the glow increases by 20.
Every 100 milliseconds, set the far of each dot to the square root of ((its x minus 22) times (its x minus 22) plus (its y minus 15) times (its y minus 15)) minus 3 times the sine of the glow.
Every 100 milliseconds, set the look of each dot to "@" if its far is under 4, otherwise "#" if its far is under 6, otherwise "o" if its far is under 8, otherwise "+" if its far is under 10, otherwise ":" if its far is under 12, otherwise "." if its far is under 15, otherwise " ".
Every 100 milliseconds, set the hue of each dot to "white" if its far is under 4, otherwise "yellow" if its far is under 10, otherwise "red".

Draw each dot as its look in its hue at its x and its y.
